      "content": "Conservative arguments often lean on the belief in the **imago Dei** (the \"in the image of God\"), which is the foundational concept that bestows absolute, inalienable worth on every human being from conception to natural death, regardless of perceived quality of life.\n\nThe explicitly **natural law tradition** is also strong, which posits that there is an objective moral order inherent in the natural world, and intentionally ending a life violates that in God's intended order for the human good. This view often strongly critiques the \"slippery slope,\" arguing that legalizing one form of aid will inevitably lead to the devaluing of all life.",
